{"assets":["/statement-assets/8b22ec8211115a13c222d35591a6b548530711b551cc186c73dba263c9deec45.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1739","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Immobile Knight"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a chess board of size $$$n \\times m$$$. The rows are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, the columns are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a cell "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"isolated"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if a knight placed in that cell can't move to any other cell on the board. Recall that a chess knight moves two cells in one direction and one cell in a perpendicular direction: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/8b22ec8211115a13c222d35591a6b548530711b551cc186c73dba263c9deec45.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"isolated"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" cell on the board. If there are no such cells, print any cell on the board."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 64$$$) — the number of testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each testcase contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m \\le 8$$$) — the number of rows and columns of the board."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, print two integers — the row and the column of any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"isolated"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" cell on the board. If there are no such cells, print any cell on the board."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 7\n8 8\n3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 7\n7 2\n2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first testcase, all cells are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"isolated"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". A knight can't move from any cell of the board to any other one. Thus, any cell on board is a correct answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second testcase, there are no "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"isolated"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" cells. On a normal chess board, a knight has at least two moves from any cell. Thus, again, any cell is a correct answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third testcase, only the middle cell of the board is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"isolated"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The knight can move freely around the border of the board, but can't escape the middle."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1739A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1739/problem/A"}